{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>The appointed seasons of YHWH which you shall proclaim as holy convocations.</b> After treating the offerings and those who offer them — whose purpose is the indwelling of the Shekhinah in Israel, as it says: עֹלַת תָּמִיד לְדֹרֹתֵיכֶם פֶּתַח אֹהֶל מוֹעֵד לִפְנֵי ה׳ אֲשֶׁר אִוָּעֵד לָכֶם שָׁמָּה (Exodus 29:42) — he now treats the appointed seasons, through whose cessation from labor he intends to rest in some of them entirely from the work of the layman, as is the case with the Sabbath and the Day of Atonement, and in all of them to engage in Torah and sacred pursuits, as it says: שֵׁשֶׁת יָמִים תַּעֲבֹד וגו׳, וְיוֹם הַשְּׁבִיעִי שַׁבָּת לַה׳ אֱלֹהֶיךָ (Exodus 20:9–10), so that you rest from your labor and all your occupation be for YHWH your Elohim. And in some of them the cessation will be from laborious work alone, as is the case with the other appointed seasons, and the intention in them is that, together with the joy of the day in which Israel rejoices in its Maker, there shall be engagement in part with sacred pursuits, as they said of blessed memory: 'A festival day — half for YHWH and half for you.' And through this the Shekhinah dwells upon Israel without doubt, as it says: אֱלֹהִים נִצָּב בַּעֲדַת אֵל (Psalms 82:1). He called them 'appointed seasons which you shall proclaim as holy convocations,' meaning gatherings of the people for sacred pursuits, for a gathering of the people is called מִקְרָא, as in חֹדֶשׁ וְשַׁבָּת קְרֹא מִקְרָא (Isaiah 1:13), and likewise עַל מְכוֹן הַר צִיּוֹן וְעַל מִקְרָאֶיהָ (Isaiah 4:5)." "<b>These are My appointed seasons.</b> They are those appointed seasons that I desire. However, when you do not proclaim them as holy convocations but they become ordinary convocations and occasions for mundane pursuits and human enjoyments alone, they are not My appointed seasons, but rather מוֹעֲדֵיכֶם שָׂנְאָה נַפְשִׁי (Isaiah 1:14)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:37:30.904221767Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}